   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "We have seen the hardware: cores, caches, coherence. Now the software that uses it. OpenMP is the standard way to parallelise C, C++ and Fortran on a shared-memory machine, with a few compiler directives."
     },
